Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Decomposition Bases", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.994947132469829*^9},ExpressionUUID->"faaca91e-d8dc-411f-91bd-\
c98c8ba743c8"],

Cell["\<\
We begin with equal external field momenta to simplify the projection bases. \
This specialization yields necessary conditions and may leave additional \
freedom. Since the identities must hold for arbitrary momenta, this \
specialization can at worst yield no useful information; it cannot produce an \
incorrect necessary condition.
The specialized system below has a one-dimensional solution space, and the \
Goldberg-Palatini action belongs to it. Once that geometric identification is \
established, the full and specialized solution spaces coincide within the \
ansatz (Section IV of the paper).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9949471382335157`*^9, 3.994947235736916*^9}, {
  3.998928948702634*^9, 3.998928949384499*^9}, {3.9989295966890717`*^9, 
  3.998929601891905*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"50bffb76-3584-4504-9f77-\
75dd04c485a5"],

