Cell["\<\
Here we use ahG and cGG as the free coefficients. In the displayed basishG \
order, ahG multiplies the first element,. After Khh = 0, this parametrizes \
the remaining relative freedom in the quadratic action; W32 sets ahG to zero. \
cGG then parametrizes the overall normalization. We store the results:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9957011372814417`*^9, 3.995701260246407*^9}, {
  3.998930242543083*^9, 3.998930255520751*^9}, {3.998930380669175*^9, 
  3.998930385107128*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6b1b1d8e-26a8-40c4-9ac8-\
cb85237c0993"],

